  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)$ be a positive function such that the area bounded by $y=f(x), y=0$ from $x=0$ to $x=a>0$ is $e^{-a}+4 a^2+a-1$. Then the differential equation, whose general solution is $y=c_1 f(x)+c_2$, where $c_1$ and $c_2$ are arbitrary constants, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EKJjf",
      "text": "$\\left(8 e^x-1\\right) \\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}+\\frac{d y}{d x}=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hfmF8",
      "text": "$\\left(8 e^x-1\\right) \\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}-\\frac{d y}{d x}=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "URujB",
      "text": "$\\left(8 e^x+1\\right) \\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}-\\frac{d y}{d x}=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "r6H8A",
      "text": "$\\left(8 e^x+1\\right) \\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}+\\frac{d y}{d x}=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\int_0^a f(x) d x=e^{-a}+4 a^2+a-1 \\\\ & f(a)=-e^{-a}+8 a+1 \\\\ & f(x)=-e^{-x}+8 x+1\\end{aligned}$\nNow $y=C_1 \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})+\\mathrm{C}_2$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\mathrm{C}_1 \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(\\mathrm{x})=\\mathrm{C}_1\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{-\\mathrm{x}}+8\\right)$   ...(1)\n$\\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}=-C_1 e^{-x} \\Rightarrow-e^x \\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}$\nPut in equation (1)\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{d y}{d x}=-e^x \\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}\\left(e^{-x}+8\\right) \\\\ & \\left(8 e^x+1\\right) \\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}+\\frac{d y}{d x}=0\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
